cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SPDB v1.0.0 — Spanish Political Discourse Annotation Resource"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-29"
message: "If you use this resource, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: dataset
license: CC-BY-4.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20745404"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cesar-andress/spanish_political_discourse_benchmark"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20745404"
abstract: >
  SPDB is a reproducible annotation resource for pragmatic-function coding in
  Spanish parliamentary discourse. Version 1.0.0 packages schemas, guidelines,
  a ParlaMint-derived development slice, a completed two-coder N=100 diagnostic
  reliability pilot (observed agreement 0.350; Cohen kappa ~0.235;
  Krippendorff alpha ~0.223; Fleiss kappa ~0.219; 65 disagreements), disagreement
  analysis, and revised codebook-v1.1.0. The revised guidelines are documented
  but have not been independently reliability-tested. This release is not an
  adjudicated gold benchmark.
keywords:
  - Spanish political discourse
  - parliamentary discourse
  - pragmatics
  - pragmatic function
  - corpus annotation
  - inter-annotator agreement
  - annotation disagreement
  - language resources
